From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd-clsh: sequence the shared headphone supply
 once

From WCD937x on, the HPHL and HPHR Class-H handlers run the same supply
sequence. Each puts the regulator in its forced-IQ startup configuration
(CLASSH_MODE_2 = 0x1c, CLASSH_MODE_3 bit 1 set, FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2
bits 7:5 = 0b101) and relies on the flyback and buck enables to move it
to the operating configuration (0x3a, bit 1 clear, 0b111). The enables are
reference counted and only act for the first user. When the second
headphone channel starts, the startup configuration is written again and
nothing leaves it while both channels are playing.

Stopping the first of two channels has the opposite problem. It returns
the HPH, flyback and buck modes to their defaults and releases the forced
IQ settings while the other channel is still playing.

Qualcomm's downstream driver avoids both by treating left plus right as a
combined state, whose transitions leave the supply alone. Do the same:
skip a v3 headphone handler while the other headphone channel is active,
so that only the first channel to start and the last one to stop
sequence the shared supply.

On an AYN Odin 3 (WCD9395), stereo headphone playback without this
change reads back CLASSH_MODE_2/CLASSH_MODE_3/FLYBACK_VNEGDAC_CTRL_2 as
0x1c/0xf2/0xb8 and warbles audibly; with the pair sequenced once they
read 0x3a/0xf0/0xf8 and the warble is gone.

Fixes: 19c5d1f6a0c3 ("ASoC: codecs: wcd-clsh: add new version support")
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
index e1465b9..6e1517d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-clsh-v2.c
@@ -544,6 +544,13 @@ static void wcd_clsh_v3_state_hph_r(struct wcd_clsh_ctrl *ctrl, int req_state,
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Both headphone channels share one supply configuration, which only
+	 * the first channel to start and the last one to stop may sequence.
+	 */
+	if (ctrl->state & WCD_CLSH_STATE_HPHL)
+		return;
+
 	if (is_enable) {
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_regulator_mode(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_mode(component, mode);
@@ -634,6 +641,13 @@ static void wcd_clsh_v3_state_hph_l(struct wcd_clsh_ctrl *ctrl, int req_state,
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Both headphone channels share one supply configuration, which only
+	 * the first channel to start and the last one to stop may sequence.
+	 */
+	if (ctrl->state & WCD_CLSH_STATE_HPHR)
+		return;
+
 	if (is_enable) {
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_buck_regulator_mode(component, mode);
 		wcd_clsh_v3_set_flyback_mode(component, mode);
